[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4128080733","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117831#issuecomment-4128080733","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117831","id":4128080733,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72DYNd","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-25T16:39:35Z","updated_at":"2026-03-25T16:39:35Z","body":"> `LocalVector<Pair<int, Variant::Type>>`\r\n\r\nThis could also be a `LocalVector<Variant::Type>`. The indices are continuous. They just don't start with zero since they are offseted by a fixed (constant per function) offset which could be stored once per function. Not sure if it would make much of a difference.\r\n\r\n> (I tried also ditching `type_init_function_table` in favor of an explicit `switch`, but saw surprisingly little gains.)\r\n\r\nWouldn't a switch just compile to something with the same structure we have in code right now :thinking:\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":