to look at the generated assembly. I just figured the array of function pointers might have have prevented inlining of the different initializers at least, but I'm probably underestimating the compiler (Clang in my case).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4128373685/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4133532849","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117831#issuecomment-4133532849","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117831","id":4133532849,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72YLSx","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T10:42:41Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T10:42:41Z","body":"The one question would be if there are any pointers to the data in this map, if not this would be safe","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4133532849/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4133900381","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117831#issuecomment-4133900381","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117831","id":4133900381,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72ZlBd","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T11:37:51Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T11:37:51Z","body":"> The one question would be if there are any pointers to the data in this map, if not this would be safe\r\n\r\nThere is not. The usage of `temporary_slots` (and its contents) is limited to just the for-loop in `GDScriptFunction::call`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4133900381/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4134579516","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117831#issuecomment-4134579516","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117831","id":4134579516,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72cK08","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T13:03:17Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T13:08:30Z","body":"> This could also be a `LocalVector<Variant::Type>`\r\n\r\nI just gave this a try, and (assuming I didn't screw anything up) it actually ended up being ever so slightly slower in our real-world project. The indices are not in fact contiguous though, since `NIL` temporaries are currently omitted from `temporary_slots`, so I'm forced to include them and then skip them in `GDScriptFunction::call`, so it could be that the branching is what made the difference.\r\n\r\n> I just figured the array of function pointers might have have prevented inlining of the different initializers at least\r\n\r\nI can confirm that this is actually happening though, even though the initializers are all `_FORCE_INLINE_`. The generated assembly (in Clang with `target=template_release optimize=speed lto=thin`) ends up being an actual `call` instruction. But again, I saw no improvement in performance with the inlined switch-cases. If anything it was maybe ever so slightly slower, but that was within margin of error.\r\n\r\nI also tried combining this with the `LocalVector<Variant::Type>` approach, and saw the same effect.\r\n\r\nSo it seems sticking with `AHashMap` (or `LocalVector<Pair<...>>`) and `type_init_function_table` is the better option here.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4134579516/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4136890496","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117831#issuecomment-4136890496","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117831","id":4136890496,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72k_CA","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T17:37:45Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T17:37:45Z","body":"So assuming there is no measurable difference I'd prefer to go with `TightLocalVector<Pair<int, Variant::Type>>` simply because we don't need any of the functionalities a map type provides.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4136890496/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4163669536","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117831#issuecomment-4163669536","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117831","id":4163669536,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74LI4g","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T15:53:42Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T15:53:42Z"